[SSL/TLS Handshake Error in Flask Server] (noted by Claude): 2026-09-04

Incident: "Bad request version" error when accessing Flask development server

Error output:
code 400, message Bad request version ('¡Ë÷R\x7f\x91øO\x99')
Garbled binary data indicates TLS ClientHello attempting HTTPS connection to HTTP server

Root cause:
Flask development server runs on plain HTTP (localhost:5000). Browser or client attempted HTTPS connection, causing protocol mismatch. TLS record header (\x16\x03\x01) indicates SSL/TLS ClientHello being sent to non-HTTPS server.

Typical causes:
1. Browser auto-upgrading to HTTPS
2. HSTS policy requiring HTTPS
3. Client configured for HTTPS only

Resolution:
1. QUICK FIX: Explicitly use http://localhost:5000 (not https://)
2. PERMANENT FIX: Add SSL/TLS support to Flask server with self-signed cert
3. ALTERNATIVE: Use environment variable to disable HTTPS auto-upgrade

Status: Not a code issue - browser/client configuration issue. Server functioning correctly on HTTP.

